  "kind": "pipeline",
  "note": "R9 spec §15.5. Both units carry a balcony and a parking space, but only u1 sells. The split therefore has to be right on BOTH sides: gross sale receipts must carry u1's 2,000,000p of ancillary and none of u2's, and the retained (unrealised) value must carry u2's 2,500,000p. A regression that summed only internal value into receipts would leave GDV and receipts disagreeing by exactly the ancillary total. The `downside` scenario is a pure −10% GDV stress (every other lever is 0) so the stressed ancillary values are hand-derivable in one step — spec §12.1 moves ancillary VALUE with GDV, and leaves ancillary AREA alone.",
